column2:
target        = where the event ORIGINATED (deepest element under the pointer).
currentTarget = the element whose listener is running — what addEventListener
                was bound to. Same for the whole handler.

Events bubble, so a click on a child still runs the parent's listener with
target = that child. To act only when the click is on the bound element itself:

  backdrop.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    if (e.target === e.currentTarget) dismiss();  // ignore clicks inside
  });

Self-contained (no free `backdrop` variable), survives refactors. Classic
modal-backdrop close: dismiss on backdrop click, keep clicks inside the box.

The browser resets event.currentTarget to null once dispatch finishes — it is
valid only during the SYNCHRONOUS run of the handler. Read it after an await or
inside a setTimeout and it is null. event.target is NOT reset; it stays valid.

  el.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
    e.currentTarget;   // the element
    await save();
    e.currentTarget;   // null!
    e.target;          // still fine
  });

Fix: capture it up front —  const self = e.currentTarget;
